DERIVED WORK — METIS (CeCILL-C)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The fast neutral-beam model is a TRANSCRIPTION of METIS, not an independent
implementation from the literature, and it is not covered by the GACODE notice
above: METIS is a different code under a different licence.

    Upstream:  METIS, the fast integrated tokamak simulator of CEA/IRFM
    Terms:     CeCILL-C (the French LGPL-compatible licence)
    Authors:   J.-F. Artaud and the METIS contributors

Files in this distribution that derive from it:

    rust/fylite/src/heating.rs            <- the TRANSCRIBED ARITHMETIC of all
                                             of the below.  It moved here from
                                             nbi.py with the single-host
                                             convergence (FYL-SDD-01
                                             DE-COMP-01); nbi.py keeps the
                                             assembly and the statement of
                                             changes, and calls this through
                                             the C ABI.

    python/fylite/scenario/model/nbi.py   <- zerod/z0nbipath.m (chord
                                             attenuation), z0nbistop.m (Janev
                                             stopping cross-section),
                                             z0signbi.m (Riviere/Janev
                                             e-impact + i-impact + CX),
                                             zicd0.m (Stix critical energy,
                                             slowing-down time, beam-driven
                                             current), zfract0.m (Wesson
                                             ion/electron power split),
                                             zsupra0.m (effective slowing time)

    rust/fylite/src/heating.rs            <- zerod/z0icrh.m (the minority ICRH
                                             chain: resonance layer and
                                             harmonic choice, Stix's analytic
                                             minority distribution and its H
                                             function, the fast-ion content
                                             and the Eriksson electron share),
                                             zerod/z0qp.m (the monotone q
                                             profile the layer search runs on)

STATEMENT OF CHANGES.  Six deliberate deviations from METIS, each stated at its
use site in nbi.py: the chord is marched on a fine path grid with psi_N read by
bilinear interpolation of the equilibrium's own psi(R,Z) rather than built from
circle-line intersections against circular surfaces; the beam is a SUM over the
full/half/third energy components an EAST positive-ion source records, not a
single injected energy; the Larmor radius is exact rather than METIS's
deuterium-calibrated constant; and the trapped fraction is Lin-Liu & Miller
rather than METIS's 0.95*sqrt(x) fallback.

The FAST-WAVE current-drive efficiency in the same file is a
transcription of `zerod/zicd0.m`'s FWCD block (a linear fit in central
electron temperature, regressed in `zerod/fitetafwcd.m` on published
measurements).  ★The driven-current PROFILE that accompanies it upstream is
NOT ported: no certification case exercises it.

The EC current-drive efficiency in the same file is a transcription of
`zerod/zicd0.m`'s efficiency block (the Giruzzi fit with Lin-Liu's Z_eff
dependence).  ★What is NOT taken from METIS there: the EC deposition
RADIUS.  Upstream takes it as an input (`cons.xece`) and lays a Gaussian on
it; this distribution computes where a launched beam meets the cold
resonance layer instead, from the launcher geometry and the field.  The
LH/EC synergy factor upstream applies to that current is not ported.

DELIBERATE DIVERGENCES IN THE ICRH CHAIN, each stated at its use site:
the plasma at the resonance layer is the CALLER's (this distribution reads
real profiles; METIS evaluates its own 0-D peaking forms there); only the
STEADY branch is transcribed (upstream's `transitoire = 1` integrates an ODE
over the discharge, which needs a time axis this function does not have); a
machine with toroidal-field ripple is REFUSED rather than answered without
the loss upstream subtracts from its own previous step; and a resonance that
falls outside the machine is refused rather than pinned to the end of the
search chord.

★RABBIT is named in that module as the FIDELITY TIER the model belongs to
(Weiland et al., Nucl. Fusion 58 (2018) 082032), not as a source: RABBIT's own
source is MPCDF-licensed and is not obtainable, so nothing here derives from it.
Saying so is the point — a reader who sees "RABBIT-class" should be able to find
out immediately that no RABBIT code was seen, let alone copied.

